The given,
$L_1=108 \mathrm{mH}, N_1=600$ turns, $N_2=500$ turns and $L_2=$ ?
By self-inductance of a plane coil $\begin{aligned}$&amp; L_1=$\frac{\mu_0 \pi N_1^2 a_1}{2}$\\
&amp; L_2=$\frac{\mu_0 \pi N_2^2 a_2}{2}
\end{aligned}$From the Eqs. (i) and (ii), we get $\begin{aligned}\frac{L_1}{L_2}$&amp; =\left(\frac{N_1}{N_2}\right)^2 \quad\left(\because$a_1=a_2\right) \\
$\frac{108}{L_2}$&amp; =\left(\frac{600}{500}\right)^2 \\
L_2 &amp; =$\frac{108 \times 25}{36}$\\
L_2 &amp; =3 $\times$25=75 $\mathrm{mH}
\end{aligned}
